# Responsive by default (Solivya)

Every UI change must keep the page usable on phone, tablet, and desktop — even when the user does not mention responsive.

## Required habits

- Design for **~360–390px** first, then **~768**, then **≥1100**. Do not ship desktop-only layouts.
- After nav, hero, grids, or spacing changes: check for **horizontal overflow**, overlapping controls, and clipped tap targets.
- Prefer **reflow** (stack / hide secondary links / wrap) over shrinking text until unreadable.
- Multi-column grids (`.split`, includes, steps, FAQ+price) must collapse cleanly under ~900px; single-column on narrow phones when content feels cramped.
- Keep primary actions reachable: brand, language toggle, **Giriş**, and main CTAs must not collide on small screens.
- Long AZ/RU strings: verify the **longest locale**, not only Azerbaijani.
- Do not rely on the user asking for a responsive check — treat it as part of finishing the change.

## Quick fail checks

```text
❌ Nav/brand/lang/login overlapping at 320–390px
❌ Page scrollWidth > viewport width
❌ Side-by-side sections that stay 2-col on phones and become unreadable
✅ Mid nav links may hide on very small screens if lang + Giriş stay visible
```
